exports[`security.habitat.redteam (contract renders) given: [case5] init guards its own args when invoked directly when: [t0] init help is requested then: it renders the init help (snapshot) 1`] = `
"🐈 heres the deal...

🧿 security.habitat.redteam init — scaffold the ward-loop route

usage:
  rhx security.habitat.redteam init --scope <path> --grain <grain> [--peers <n>] [--budget <n>] [--skip-route-bind]

args:
  --scope <path>      the habitat surface to sweep (required)
  --grain <grain>     one of infil,exfil,leak,all (required)
                      infil = what reaches in · exfil = what can leave, by any outbound channel · leak = what your own next push publishes · all = the three
  --peers <n>         blind peers per grain-partition, 1 to 9999 (default: 3)
  --budget <n>        the loop's spend allowance, 1 to 9999 cycles (default: 1 — one pass, no re-detect)
  --skip-route-bind   scaffold the route but do not bind it to the branch

what it does:
  1. creates route at <repo root>/.behavior/v<date>.guardian-redteam.grain=<grain>[.scope=<token>]/
     (the slug folds in the grain — and a scope token for a subtree — so two same-day sweeps get distinct routes)
  2. copies the ward-loop .stone + .guard files
  3. stands up a gitignored claims path (live claims never publish)
  4. binds route to the current branch (unless --skip-route-bind)

exit: 0 = scaffolded · 1 = malfunction · 2 = constraint

⚠️ informational only — not professional security advice, not exhaustive; consult a qualified security professional for your own habitat
"
`;

