exports[`security.habitat.redteam (halt renders) given: [case38] a two-cycle budget, and a retried cycle when: [t0] the plan prices a budget of 2 then: it says cycle 2 re-detects cycle 1's repairs 1`] = `
"🐈 chartin course...

🧿 security.habitat.redteam --mode plan --scope . --grain leak --peers 3 --budget 2
   ├─ scope: .
   ├─ grains: leak  (1 grain-partition, disjoint by grain-surface)
   ├─ peers: 3 per grain-partition  ⇒ 3 blind peers total
   ├─ budget: 2 loop cycles — each draws one detect → verify → repair pass
   ├─ re-detect: cycle 2 re-detects cycle 1's repairs; cycle 2's repairs stay PENDING-REDETECT
   ├─ projected: 3 peers × 2 cycles = up to 6 peer-dispatch runs
   ├─ a bound route: apply keeps its recorded peers + budget for any flag this request omits; a new --peers is refused once 1.ground cuts the slices
   ├─ the ward loop: ground → detect → verify → repair → promote → (loop | terminate)
   ├─ publishes: 5.promote opens a public gh issue on ehmpathy/rhachet-roles-ghlitch per fullsun-safe lesson (a generalized class, never a live claim); each push runs the dispatch-lesson scan gate first, and live claims stay in .claims/
   ├─ defers: 4.repair never revokes or rotates a credential at its issuer — it drafts the command for a human to run, and the claim stays open until the human returns its output
   ├─ rewrites: 4.repair edits the tree and rewrites each local unpushed commit that carries a leaked value — each rewrite passes rhx security.habitat.redteam backup-before-rewrite first, which takes a backup ref (refs/redteam-backup/<branch>.<head-sha>, never pushed by --all) and refuses the rewrite when the tree holds uncommitted work
   ├─ per-peer slices: 3 per grain-partition, cut by 1.ground at drive time into .claims/1.ground.yield.md — its guard grades them, and the drive goes on to 2.detect with no pause; this plan is your read before the spend
   ├─ scope limit: blind peers cannot see the aggregate map (a leak only the whole published set forms); a clean verdict does not clear it — review the whole corpus for that class apart
   ├─ per-grain prompts (each peer is blind to the others' slice + theory)
   │  ├─ leak  — "what value on this slice is already exposed, or forms a map with others?"
   │  └─ each claim = a chain (entry/exit → mechanism → blast radius|audience), keyed on channel+mechanism
   └─ next: spend it: rhx security.habitat.redteam --scope . --grain leak --peers 3 --budget 2 --mode apply

⚠️ informational only — not professional security advice, not exhaustive; consult a qualified security professional for your own habitat
"
`;

