exports[`security.habitat.redteam (halt renders) given: [case41] the backup-before-rewrite gate, on real repos when: [t7] the gate is asked for --help then: it renders the skill page, which names the gate (exit 0) 1`] = `
"🐈 heres the deal...

🧿 security.habitat.redteam — hunt a habitat the way an adversary would

   the ward loop: ground → detect → verify → repair → promote → (loop | terminate)

usage:
  rhx security.habitat.redteam init --scope <path> --grain <grain> [--peers <n>] [--budget <n>] [--skip-route-bind]
  rhx security.habitat.redteam --scope <path> --grain <grain> [--peers <n>] [--budget <n>] --mode plan
  rhx security.habitat.redteam --scope <path> --grain <grain> [--peers <n>] [--budget <n>] [--skip-route-bind] --mode apply

ward-loop gates (the stones invoke these; never the raw command they guard):
  rhx security.habitat.redteam backup-before-rewrite                     (4.repair, before each history rewrite)
  printf '%s' "$body" | rhx security.habitat.redteam dispatch-lesson --title <title>
  rhx security.habitat.redteam rewind-detect --route <route> --cycle <n> <<'KEYS'
  <each open key, one per line, written out in full>
  KEYS

options:
  --scope            habitat surface to sweep (a repo, a subtree)         (required)
  --grain            infil | exfil | leak | all                           (required)
                     infil = what reaches in · exfil = what can leave, by any outbound channel · leak = what your own next push publishes · all = the three
  --peers            blind peers per grain-partition, 1 to 9999           (default: 3; apply to a bound route: its own; fixed once 1.ground cuts the slices)
  --budget           loop spend allowance, 1 to 9999 cycles               (default: 1 — one pass, no re-detect; apply to a bound route: its own)
  --mode             plan | apply                                         (required, except for init)
  --skip-route-bind  scaffold without a branch bind                       (apply + init only)

gate options (each gate reads only its own; any other flag belays):
  --title            dispatch-lesson: the lesson's title, '<class>: <fix>' (required)
  --route            rewind-detect: the route dir under .behavior/        (required)
  --cycle            rewind-detect: the cycle just walked, 1 to 9999      (required)

exit: 0 = done · 1 = malfunction · 2 = constraint

⚠️ informational only — not professional security advice, not exhaustive; consult a qualified security professional for your own habitat
"
`;

